id: pm-beads-cg9v
title: The mandatory docstring gate could skip its own scan and still exit zero
description: "isMainInvocation resolved this module's own path inside a try block that swallowed every failure and returned false. Returning false leaves main() unreached and process.exitCode at zero, so a release could pass the mandatory docstring gate having scanned nothing. The two resolutions now differ: an unresolvable argv[1] still answers false because that is the ordinary imported-by-a-test case, while an unresolvable own module path throws. A regression test asserts the throw and was mutation-checked by reverting the fix, which makes it fail."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-09T12:55:44.939Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-09T12:57:16.035Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-09T12:57:16.023Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-09T12:57:16.023Z"
author: claude
resolution: fixed
expected_result: A docstring gate whose own path cannot be resolved must fail the release rather than exit zero having scanned nothing.
actual_result: isMainInvocation throws on self-resolution failure; a regression test asserts the throw and the suite passes.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T12:57:15.613Z",claude,"Mutation-checked in pm-slack by reverting the split resolution back to the single try block, which makes the new test fail; the identical fix and test ship here."
close_reason: "Split the two path resolutions so only an unresolvable argv[1] answers false; an unresolvable own module path now throws."
body: ""
